<title>POLAND: Poland C/A deficit at $899 mln in January.</title>
<headline>Poland C/A deficit at $899 mln in January.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $899 million in January against a $139 million shortfall in January 1996, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	  JANUARY     DEC 1996    JAN 1996</p>
<p> current account million USD	   -899	  -368	   -139</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance     -1,476	  -958	   -661</p>
<p> exports				1,905	 2,447	  1,737</p>
<p> imports				3,381	 3,405	  2,398</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	 413	   485	    570</p>
<p>Note: Unclassified flows encompass mainly unregistered cross-border trade flows.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
